---
/*
  Consent gate for the Google Maps embed.

  Google's map sets cookies (NID and friends) the moment the iframe enters the
  document, and the CNIL treats those as requiring prior consent. So the site
  carries this bar for exactly one reason: it is the only third party on the
  page. There is no analytics, no advertising, no tag manager — and the copy
  says so, because a banner that overstates what it covers trains people to
  dismiss it.

  The choice is stored in localStorage, not a cookie: nothing is written until
  the visitor has actually chosen, which is the point.
*/
---

<div
  data-consent
  hidden
  class="fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-[60] border-t border-rule bg-surface/98 backdrop-blur-md"
  role="dialog"
  aria-labelledby="consent-title"
  aria-describedby="consent-body"
>
  <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-6xl flex-col gap-4 px-5 py-5 lg:flex-row lg:items-center lg:justify-between lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <p id="consent-title" class="font-display text-base font-bold text-ink">
        Afficher la carte Google&nbsp;?
      </p>
      <p id="consent-body" class="mt-1 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-steel">
        La carte est fournie par Google, qui dépose des cookies. C'est le seul
        service tiers de ce site&nbsp;: aucune mesure d'audience, aucune publicité.
        Si vous refusez, l'adresse et l'itinéraire restent accessibles.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex shrink-0 gap-3">
      <button
        type="button"
        data-consent-accept
        class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center bg-crimson px-6 py-3 font-display font-bold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-crimson-deep"
      >
        Accepter
      </button>
      <button
        type="button"
        data-consent-refuse
        class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center border border-rule-strong px-6 py-3 font-display font-semibold text-ink transition-colors hover:border-ink"
      >
        Refuser
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
